    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🧠 AI-Assisted SSH Command Executor (Headless-Safe)\n\nThis workflow allows users to send **Linux commands via chat**, which are then:\n\n### 🔹 Command Intelligence Layer\n- Intercepted by an AI agent before execution\n- Automatically detects and fixes broken or unsafe syntax\n- Corrects common mistakes (e.g. missing NFS colons, interactive commands)\n- Enforces **headless-safe execution**\n  - No interactive prompts\n  - No TTY-dependent behavior\n  - Pager-free output\n  - Adds non-interactive flags where required (e.g. `sudo -n`)\n\n### 🔹 Execution Layer\n- Commands are executed on a **Debian Bookworm AI Server**\n- Uses a **bash shell** via SSH\n- Designed for unattended, automation-safe operation\n\n### 🔹 Output Normalization\n- Captures `stdout`, `stderr`, exit `code`, and `signal`\n- Reformats output for chat consumption\n- Ensures each field is rendered on its own line\n- Preserves multiline output for readability\n\n### 🔒 Design Principles\n- Deterministic execution\n- Least-privilege sudo usage\n- Headless-first command design\n- Safe for AI-driven infrastructure operations\n\n### 🛠 Common Use Cases\n- Server health checks\n- Security monitoring (Fail2Ban, services)\n- Package maintenance\n- Diagnostics and observability\n- AI-assisted command correction\n\n> **Conceptually:**  \n> Humans speak loosely → AI tightens syntax → servers respond cleanly\n",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 688,
        "color": 6
      },
